# Example environment file for tb-streamer.
#
# Copy to ONE of:
#   ~/.threadbase/.env   — read by the launchd-supervised prod instance, and the
#                          only location a supervised instance can find (its cwd
#                          is /, not the repo). Survives a deploy.
#   <repo>/.env          — read by a hand-run `tb-streamer serve` via
#                          `dotenv/config` in cli/index.ts, which resolves .env
#                          from the process cwd.
#
# Never commit a filled-in copy. `.env` is gitignored; this example is not,
# because it contains no values.
#
# An explicitly exported variable always wins over the file.

# ─── iOS Live Activity push (APNs) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional as a whole: with none of these set, the server boots normally and
# Live Activity push stays off. See docs/guides/live-activity-push.md.

# The p8 signing key CONTENTS (PEM), not a path.
#
# Prefer NOT to put the key here. Drop the file at
# ~/.threadbase/AuthKey_<keyId>.p8 (chmod 600) instead — the launchd shim
# discovers it by pattern and derives APNS_KEY_ID from the filename, so a key
# rotation is a drop-in with no config change. Set this only if you need to
# supply the key by value.
#
# A multi-line PEM must be double-quoted with literal \n escapes to survive a
# single line, which is another reason the key file is the easier path.
#APNS_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----"

# Key id of the p8 above. Derived from the AuthKey_<keyId>.p8 filename when the
# key file is used, so it normally needs no setting.
#APNS_KEY_ID=

# Apple Developer team id. Required whenever APNS_KEY is set — there is no
# default, so one deployment's Apple account is never baked into the source.
#APNS_TEAM_ID=

# App bundle id. The APNs topic is this plus `.push-type.liveactivity`, and the
# signing key must be Team Scoped (All Topics) to sign it.
#APNS_BUNDLE_ID=

# APNs host. Defaults to sandbox, matching an app whose aps-environment is
# `development`. Set to api.push.apple.com for a production-signed build — a
# mismatch here is the most common reason pushes silently never arrive.
#APNS_HOST=api.sandbox.push.apple.com
